WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.920
Hey Wisecrack! Jared here.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.280
And today we're talking about the 
happiest show in the Netflix's catalogue

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.540
BoJack Horseman.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.340
With its colorful animation, talking animals, and Hollywood glamour

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.720
BoJack might look like your
typical happy-go-lucky cartoon

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.600
but this is far from the case.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.180
The show’s light hearted veneer hides a dark

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.040
and downright depressing reality

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.760
which is fitting given its focus on the disillusionment
that inevitably comes

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.500
when you look beneath the surface.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:36.240
BoJack reveals the ugly, narcissistic reality that lies behind the dazzling façade of Hollywoo.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.380
BoJack: "Most important thing is you gotta give the people what they want."

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.700
"Even if it KILLS you."

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.500
"Even if it empties you out until there's
nothing left to empty."

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.400
From Mr. Peanutbutter's feigned interest

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.180
"I wanna talk to you..."

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.520
"...ERICKA!"

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.820
to studio executives only focused on money

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.700
to meaningless award ceremonies that only
reward those with established names.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:55.460
In other words:

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.120
Charlotte: “Hollywoo’s a real pretty town that’s"

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.400
"smack on top of all that black tar."

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.140
"By the time you realize you’re sinking"

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.040
"it’s too late.”

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.720
But the show goes far deeper.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:07.120
Hollywoo could be considered a metaphor for
existence in general.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.680
Just like the façade of Hollywoo covers up the reality

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.400
of an ugly, hollow industry

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.560
the trappings of our daily lives cover up the
meaninglessness of existence itself.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.000
This idea, known as

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.300
“Existential Nihilism”

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.200
is foundational to “BoJack Horseman.”

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.520
If life is truly meaningless then how are we supposed to deal with it?

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.960
Welcome to this Wisecrack Edition on: The philosophy of “BoJack Horseman.”

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.480
What does it know? Does it know things? Let's find out!

